<title>MALAYSIA: KL tin market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>KL tin market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuala Lumpur tin market is closed on Monday for a Hindu festival. It reopens on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, tin price climbed eight cents to 14.70 ringgit ($5.83) a kg on strong Japanese buying after a higher London Metal Exchange (LME).</p>
<p>Turnover was 130 tonnes against 162 on Thursday.</p>
<p>The local premium against London rose to $50 a tonne on Friday from $30 previously.</p>
